  "report": "# Ledger benchmark report\n\nGenerated by `python -m ledger.bench` on 2026-10-13.\nEnvironment: Python 3.14.0, SQLite 3.50.4,\nWindows 11 AMD64. Database: file-backed SQLite, WAL, `synchronous=FULL`\nunless noted. Latency is per `create_payment` call through the service layer (no HTTP).\n\n## Transfers by concurrency\n\n| threads | transfers | transfers/s | postings/s | p50 ms | p95 ms | p99 ms | invariants + conservation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 4000 | 556.2 | 1112.5 | 1.49 | 2.327 | 14.752 | yes |\n| 2 | 4000 | 428.2 | 856.4 | 3.981 | 8.389 | 19.163 | yes |\n| 4 | 4000 | 426.1 | 852.2 | 8.045 | 20.566 | 25.858 | yes |\n| 8 | 4000 | 420.2 | 840.4 | 16.877 | 31.592 | 36.322 | yes |\n| 16 | 4000 | 425.3 | 850.6 | 34.5 | 50.377 | 54.722 | yes |\n\nSQLite has a single writer, so threads queue on the write lock: throughput does not scale with\nthreads (556.2 -> 425.3 transfers/s\nfrom 1 to 16 threads) and p99 grows with queue depth.\nSame single-thread load with `synchronous=NORMAL`\n(fsync at checkpoint only): 796.1 transfers/s, p99 15.962 ms.\n\n## Payment lifecycle and idempotency\n\n- authorize (hold) p50 1.094 ms / p99 2.245 ms;\n  capture p50 1.387 ms / p99 6.088 ms\n- idempotent replay p50 0.073 ms vs first write p50 1.667 ms;\n  1000/1000 retries served from the stored response\n- overdraft guard: 7 holds of 1/7 of the balance accepted,\n  3 rejected with `insufficient_funds`\n\n## Reconciliation\n\nStandard injection rates, period 2026-09-01..2026-09-30: 1633 ledger movements on\nthe cash account vs 1632 bank lines; auto-match rate\n93.51%; 138 breaks; difference\n3732848 minor units, of which 3732848 explained by\nclassified breaks (unexplained: 0). Matching took\n9.42 ms.\n\n| break type | injected | detected | correct | precision | recall |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| timing | 49 | 49 | 49 | 1.0 | 1.0 |\n| amount_mismatch | 24 | 24 | 24 | 1.0 | 1.0 |\n| duplicate | 16 | 16 | 16 | 1.0 | 1.0 |\n| missing_in_bank | 33 | 33 | 33 | 1.0 | 1.0 |\n| missing_in_ledger | 16 | 16 | 16 | 1.0 | 1.0 |\n\nStress rates (4x breaks; 35% of bank memos stripped of the reference, which settle 0-3 days\nlate, so some fall outside the 1-day matching tolerance with no reference to fall back on): precision\n0.5394, recall 0.7008, unexplained difference\n0.\n\n| break type | injected | detected | correct | precision | recall |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| timing | 433 | 196 | 196 | 1.0 | 0.4527 |\n| amount_mismatch | 98 | 98 | 98 | 1.0 | 1.0 |\n| duplicate | 65 | 65 | 65 | 1.0 | 1.0 |\n| missing_in_bank | 131 | 368 | 131 | 0.356 | 1.0 |\n| missing_in_ledger | 65 | 302 | 65 | 0.2152 | 1.0 |\n"
