  "report": "# Credit underwriting model - validation report\n\nGenerated by `python -m credit.run` (seed 20261013). All figures are from that run.\n\n## Data\n\n- 60,000 synthetic applications; development months 0-17\n  (44,852, split 31,416 train / 13,436\n  in-time holdout), out-of-time months 18-23 (15,148).\n- Bad rate: development 11.81%, out-of-time 14.51%.\n- Protected group B share: 30.0%. Used only for fairness testing.\n\n## Discrimination\n\n| Model | Sample | AUC | Gini | KS |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Scorecard (champion) | in-time holdout | 0.7074 | 0.4149 | 0.3056 |\n| Scorecard (champion) | out-of-time | 0.6997 | 0.3994 | 0.2958 |\n| GBM (challenger) | in-time holdout | 0.7020 | 0.4041 | 0.3025 |\n| GBM (challenger) | out-of-time | 0.6969 | 0.3937 | 0.2910 |\n\nChallenger OOT AUC uplift vs champion: -0.0028\n(threshold to adopt: +0.020). Decision: **WoE scorecard**.\n\n## Calibration (champion, out-of-time)\n\nMean predicted PD 12.83% vs observed\n14.51% (observed/predicted\n1.131).\n\n| Decile (1 = riskiest) | N | Predicted PD | Observed | Obs/Pred |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 1514 | 32.83% | 34.68% | 1.06 |\n| 2 | 1515 | 21.67% | 23.96% | 1.11 |\n| 3 | 1515 | 17.06% | 19.08% | 1.12 |\n| 4 | 1515 | 14.00% | 15.25% | 1.09 |\n| 5 | 1515 | 11.49% | 15.31% | 1.33 |\n| 6 | 1514 | 9.52% | 10.83% | 1.14 |\n| 7 | 1515 | 7.84% | 8.91% | 1.14 |\n| 8 | 1515 | 6.29% | 7.33% | 1.17 |\n| 9 | 1515 | 4.77% | 5.81% | 1.22 |\n| 10 | 1515 | 2.89% | 3.96% | 1.37 |\n\n## Stability\n\nScore PSI development vs out-of-time: 0.0171 (stable).\n\n## Information Value and characteristic stability\n\n| Feature | IV | Strength | Bins | In model | Coef | CSI dev->OOT |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| revolving_utilization | 0.1690 | medium | 10 | yes | -0.841 | 0.0365 |\n| credit_history_months | 0.1343 | medium | 8 | yes | -0.730 | 0.0005 |\n| employment_years | 0.1171 | medium | 8 | yes | -0.416 | 0.0003 |\n| dti | 0.1040 | medium | 9 | yes | -0.716 | 0.0013 |\n| annual_income | 0.1001 | medium | 9 | yes | -0.914 | 0.0002 |\n| delinq_2y | 0.0711 | weak | 2 | yes | -0.794 | 0.0012 |\n| inquiries_6m | 0.0491 | weak | 4 | yes | -0.799 | 0.0643 |\n| loan_amount | 0.0372 | weak | 8 | no |  | 0.0007 |\n| purpose | 0.0229 | weak | 7 | yes | -1.116 | 0.0002 |\n| term_months | 0.0130 | unpredictive | 2 | yes | -0.951 | 0.0001 |\n\nFeatures removed for a wrong-signed coefficient: loan_amount.\n\n## Fair lending (out-of-time, at each model's profit cutoff)\n\n| Model | OOT AUC | Cutoff | Approve A | Approve B | AIR | 4/5 rule | EO gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| With region (proxy) | 0.7106 | 555 | 69.7% | 52.5% | 0.753 | FAIL | 0.1582 |\n| Region removed | 0.6997 | 555 | 65.6% | 60.0% | 0.914 | pass | 0.0433 |\n| GBM challenger (matched approval) | 0.6969 | n/a | 65.9% | 59.3% | 0.900 | pass | 0.0530 |\n\nAIR = approval rate of group B / approval rate of group A; the four-fifths rule flags\nAIR < 0.80. EO gap = approval rate among good (non-defaulting) applicants, A minus B.\nRemoving the region proxy costs 0.0109 OOT AUC\n(tolerance 0.015); mitigation adopted: True.\n\n## Cutoff strategy (champion, out-of-time)\n\nUnit economics: lifetime margin 0.09, LGD\n0.70, EAD fraction 0.75;\nbreak-even PD 0.1463 (score 552.7).\n\n| Cutoff | Approval | Bad rate | Exp. loss rate | Realised loss rate | Exp. profit | Realised profit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 500 | 99.8% | 14.38% | 5.98% | 6.90% | $4,458,742.28 | $2,045,752.50 |\n| 510 | 99.1% | 14.17% | 5.90% | 6.83% | $4,651,718.82 | $2,234,775.00 |\n| 520 | 97.0% | 13.64% | 5.69% | 6.62% | $5,110,945.75 | $2,732,955.00 |\n| 530 | 92.3% | 12.61% | 5.30% | 6.24% | $5,892,531.46 | $3,570,255.00 |\n| 540 | 84.2% | 11.38% | 4.76% | 5.67% | $6,731,897.26 | $4,620,330.00 |\n| 550 | 71.5% | 9.75% | 4.08% | 4.99% | $7,259,310.65 | $5,438,887.50 |\n| 560 | 56.4% | 8.15% | 3.40% | 4.20% | $7,080,514.90 | $5,754,607.50 |\n| 570 | 40.0% | 6.49% | 2.76% | 3.41% | $6,099,527.28 | $5,290,402.50 |\n| 580 | 24.8% | 5.32% | 2.16% | 2.74% | $4,469,870.32 | $3,995,407.50 |\n| 590 | 13.3% | 4.38% | 1.66% | 2.23% | $2,777,535.61 | $2,512,530.00 |\n| 600 | 6.2% | 3.50% | 1.26% | 1.58% | $1,489,204.43 | $1,415,340.00 |\n| 610 | 2.2% | 1.47% | 0.93% | 0.56% | $597,419.30 | $630,577.50 |\n| 620 | 0.7% | 0.00% | 0.71% | 0.00% | $204,246.63 | $225,090.00 |\n\nProfit cutoff (chosen on the in-time holdout): **555**. On the OOT sample it\napproves 63.9% with a 9.05% bad rate and a\nrealised profit of $5,612,880.00, vs\n$1,899,750.00 if every applicant were approved\n(bad rate 14.51%).\n\n## Adverse action reasons (OOT declines at the profit cutoff)\n\n5,473 declined applicants;\n5,473 received four reasons.\n\n| Code | Statement | Primary | Primary % | In top 4 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R06 | Length of credit history insufficient | 1317 | 24.1% | 4764 |\n| R01 | Income insufficient for amount of credit requested | 1644 | 30.0% | 4634 |\n| R03 | Proportion of revolving balances to credit limits too high | 2083 | 38.1% | 4321 |\n| R02 | Excessive obligations in relation to income | 410 | 7.5% | 4188 |\n| R04 | Delinquent past or present credit obligations with others | 0 | 0.0% | 1334 |\n| R05 | Number of recent inquiries on credit bureau report | 5 | 0.1% | 1283 |\n| R07 | Length of employment | 0 | 0.0% | 747 |\n| R10 | Purpose of loan | 14 | 0.3% | 620 |\n| R09 | Requested repayment term | 0 | 0.0% | 1 |\n\nSample notices:\n\n- Application 44856 (score 542.7):\n  1. R03 Proportion of revolving balances to credit limits too high (32.1 points)\n  2. R06 Length of credit history insufficient (23.6 points)\n  3. R02 Excessive obligations in relation to income (21.0 points)\n  4. R01 Income insufficient for amount of credit requested (11.1 points)\n- Application 44863 (score 541.4):\n  1. R03 Proportion of revolving balances to credit limits too high (32.1 points)\n  2. R06 Length of credit history insufficient (23.6 points)\n  3. R07 Length of employment (12.9 points)\n  4. R02 Excessive obligations in relation to income (12.0 points)\n- Application 44865 (score 547.4):\n  1. R06 Length of credit history insufficient (27.6 points)\n  2. R03 Proportion of revolving balances to credit limits too high (14.5 points)\n  3. R07 Length of employment (12.9 points)\n  4. R01 Income insufficient for amount of credit requested (11.1 points)\n"
